 {"edgeAttributes":[{"po":288,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":288,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Antunes Lab"}, {"po":288,"n":"name","v":"Node 1 (interacts with) PROTEAN-CR"}, {"po":288,"n":"Why?","v":"Integration with PROTEAN-CR will put CrossDome on a hub for tools and researchers interested in developing vaccines and immunotherapies."}, {"po":289,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":289,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Antunes Lab"}, {"po":289,"n":"name","v":"Node 1 (interacts with) pVACTools"}, {"po":289,"n":"Why?","v":"The integration of CrossDome with HLA-Arena will enable comprehensive evaluation of peptide-HLA binding alongside cross-reactivity prediction. This connection is vital for refining target selection by providing a complete picture of a candidate's potential immunogenicity and off-target effects, leading to improved therapeutic design."}, {"po":276,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":276,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tin Nguyen"}, {"po":276,"n":"name","v":"CytoAnalyst (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":276,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-025-14398-x"}, {"po":276,"n":"Why?","v":"CytoAnalyst uses many Bioconductor packages, such as rhdf5, MAST, and slingshot, to perform single-cell analysis"}, {"po":275,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":275,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tin Nguyen"}, {"po":275,"n":"name","v":"IPSA (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":275,"n":"Why?","v":"IPSA uses Bioconductor packages, such as limma, fgsea, padog."}, {"po":285,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":285,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alexander Krasnitz"}, {"po":285,"n":"name","v":"RAIDS (interacts with) Galaxy"}, {"po":274,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":274,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alexander Krasnitz"}, {"po":274,"n":"name","v":"RAIDS connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":274,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/RAIDS.html"}, {"po":274,"n":"Why?","v":"Bioconductor currently is the main platform for hosting RAIDS, facilitating its download and installation, and providing its documentation."}, {"po":273,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":273,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pablo G. Camara"}, {"po":273,"n":"name","v":"ImmunoPheno (interacts with) Galaxy"}, {"po":273,"n":"Why?","v":"ImmunoPheno is a Python package and online resource that leverages existing single-cell proteo-transcriptomic atlases of human tissues to automate the design, annotation, and gating of multiplexed antibody-based cytometry experiments. To improve ImmunoPheno's accessibility, interoperability with existing single-cell RNA-seq and cytometry analysis tools, and to enhance workflow transparency and reproducibility, key functionalities have also been implemented onto Galaxy, an open-source, web-based platform for accessible, reproducible, and transparent high-throughput biological data analysis."}, {"po":272,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":272,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Yufei Huang"}, {"po":272,"n":"name","v":"m6A-Suite (connected with) NDEx"}, {"po":272,"n":"Why?","v":"m6A-Suite will leverage NDEx networks to elucidate m6A functions in cancer and  use NDEx to host the m6A regulatory networks"}, {"po":271,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":271,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":271,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) TCPA"}, {"po":271,"n":"Why?","v":"Retrieve information regarding functional proteomics data of patient tumor and cell line samples to be used in PROTEAN-CR"}, {"po":270,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":270,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":270,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":270,"n":"Why?","v":"Recover the most frequent mutation by gene and use this information to modify input receptors in PROTEAN-CR"}, {"po":269,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":269,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":269,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":269,"n":"Why?","v":"A simplified PROTEAN-CR module will be deployed as one of the analysis tools available in OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":268,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":268,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":268,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) CIViC"}, {"po":268,"n":"Why?","v":"Use PROTEAN-CR as an interface to access CIViC variants in cancer proteins"}, {"po":267,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":267,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":267,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) pVACTools"}, {"po":267,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://proteancr.kavrakilab.rice.edu/"}, {"po":267,"n":"Why?","v":"Search for neoantigens in a given sequence and export these results back to PROTEAN-CR to model it in the context of different HLAs"}, {"po":266,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":266,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lydia Kavraki"}, {"po":266,"n":"name","v":"PROTEAN-CR (connected with) CEDAR"}, {"po":266,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/KavrakiLab/protean-cr-connections"}, {"po":266,"n":"Why?","v":"CEDAR is a cancer epitope database that catalogs experimental data on antibody and T cell peptidic epitopes. These datasets however are mostly sequence-based, containing the sequence of the peptide, but not structural information. PROTEAN-CR consists of tools such as APE-Gen2.0 that, given an amino-acid sequence of a peptide and an MHC type, can rapidly provide a peptide-MHC structural model. There is potential in connecting such databases with structural modeling tools to also provide structural models that can provide additional information in selecting peptide candidates in cancer immunotherapy applications."}, {"po":257,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":257,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Harry Hochheiser"}, {"po":257,"n":"name","v":"CLAMP-Cancer (connected with) DeepPhe"}, {"po":257,"n":"Why?","v":"Exchange of NLP methods"}, {"po":256,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":256,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Xiaoqian Jiang"}, {"po":256,"n":"name","v":"GEARBOx (connected with) mCODEGPT"}, {"po":256,"n":"Why?","v":"By integrating GEARBox with mCodeGPT, we can tackle a major data standardization challenge by automatically linking clinical trial narratives to patient profiles. This addresses the difficulty in matching patients with relevant trials based on heterogeneous trial data."}, {"po":255,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":255,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Joshua Campbell"}, {"po":255,"n":"name","v":"musicatk (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":255,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/musicatk.html"}, {"po":255,"n":"Why?","v":"Bioconductor is a repository for R packages"}, {"po":254,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":254,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Joshua Campbell"}, {"po":254,"n":"name","v":"musicatk (connected with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":254,"n":"Why?","v":"musicatk will perform systematic mutational signature analysis on studies in cBioPortal"}, {"po":253,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":253,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Guilherme Del Fiol "}, {"po":253,"n":"name","v":"mCODEGPT (connected with) GARDE"}, {"po":253,"n":"Why?","v":"Extract cancer family history from unstructured clinical notes in the electronic health record using large language models to help identify patients who meet criteria for genetic testing of hereditary cancer."}, {"po":277,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":277,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":277,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) UCSC Genome Browser"}, {"po":277,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12026984/"}, {"po":277,"n":"Why?","v":"The iPepGen pipeline outputs information on identified neoantigen peptides that includes URL links for direct viewing of genomic and transcriptomic evidence in the UCSC Browser"}, {"po":252,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":252,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":252,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) Galaxy-P multi-omics"}, {"po":252,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12026984/"}, {"po":252,"n":"Why?","v":"Proteogenomic tools available in Galaxy-P have been adapted for immunopeptidogenomic workflows "}, {"po":251,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":251,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":251,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) Galaxy"}, {"po":251,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12026984/"}, {"po":251,"n":"Why?","v":"The iPepGen pipeline in implemented in Galaxy and uses latest features for workflow development, dissemination and training."}, {"po":250,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":250,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":250,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) IGV"}, {"po":250,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12026984/"}, {"po":250,"n":"Why?","v":"The iPepGen pipeline outputs results files on identified neoantigen peptides that are compatible with viewing and interpretation using IGV"}, {"po":249,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":249,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":249,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) pVACTools"}, {"po":249,"n":"Why?","v":"Work is ongoing to integrate tools from pVacTools for prioritizing identified neoantigen peptides for further experimental validation"}, {"po":248,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":248,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tim Griffin"}, {"po":248,"n":"name","v":"iPepGen (connected with) CEDAR"}, {"po":248,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12026984/"}, {"po":248,"n":"Why?","v":"The iPepGen pipeline utilizes tools available in CEDAR for prediction of neoantigen peptide binding to HLA alleles and immunogenicity potential"}, {"po":278,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":278,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Levi Waldron"}, {"po":278,"n":"name","v":"spatialGE (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":278,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/FridleyLab/spatialGE/blob/main/DESCRIPTION"}, {"po":278,"n":"Why?","v":"The spatialGE R package utilizes Bioconductor packages including BiocParallel, DelayedArray, GSVA, scSpacialSIM, and msigdbr."}, {"po":243,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":243,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Brooke L. Fridley"}, {"po":243,"n":"name","v":"spatialGE (connected with) WebMeV"}, {"po":243,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://webmev.tm4.org/about"}, {"po":243,"n":"Why?","v":"WebMeV facilitates user-friendly access to spatialGE, an R package for the analysis of spatial transcriptomics data. With this integration, users can run spatialGE analyses without command-line usage and/or scripting."}, {"po":242,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":242,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Brooke L. Fridley"}, {"po":242,"n":"name","v":"spatialGE (connected with) GenePattern"}, {"po":242,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://genepattern.github.io/spatialGE.STenrich/v1/"}, {"po":242,"n":"Why?","v":"GenePattern facilitates user-friendly access to spatialGE, an R package for the analysis of spatial transcriptomics data. With this integration, users can run spatialGE analyses without command-line usage and/or scripting."}, {"po":241,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":241,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Brooke L. Fridley"}, {"po":241,"n":"name","v":"DEGAS (connected with) spatialGE"}, {"po":241,"n":"Why?","v":"The spatialGE web application facilitates user-friendly access to DEGAS, an algorithm applying transfer learning of disease information from patients to cells in spatial transcriptomics data. With this integration, users can run DEGAS without command-line usage and/or scripting."}, {"po":240,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":240,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Brooke L. Fridley"}, {"po":240,"n":"name","v":"CalicoST (connected with) spatialGE"}, {"po":240,"n":"Why?","v":"The spatialGE web application facilitates user-friendly access to CalicoST, an algorithm to infer copy number variations from spatial transcriptomics data. With this integration, users can run CalicoST without command-line usage and/or scripting."}, {"po":265,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":265,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Spyridon Bakas"}, {"po":265,"n":"name","v":"GaNDLF (connected with) XNAT"}, {"po":265,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://docs.mlcommons.org/GaNDLF/itcr_connectivity/#xnat"}, {"po":265,"n":"Why?","v":"Enable the use of GaNDLF's models to databases and population cohorts defined by XNAT."}, {"po":264,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":264,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Spyridon Bakas"}, {"po":264,"n":"name","v":"GaNDLF (connected with) OHIF"}, {"po":264,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://docs.mlcommons.org/GaNDLF/itcr_connectivity/#ohif"}, {"po":264,"n":"Why?","v":"Online visualization of images"}, {"po":263,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":263,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Spyridon Bakas"}, {"po":263,"n":"name","v":"GaNDLF (connected with) RADIOMICS.io"}, {"po":263,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://docs.mlcommons.org/GaNDLF/itcr_connectivity/#radiomics"}, {"po":263,"n":"Why?","v":"Extraction of downstream features of automatically generated segmentation maps using Radiomics.io."}, {"po":262,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":262,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Spyridon Bakas"}, {"po":262,"n":"name","v":"GaNDLF (connected with) RADxTools"}, {"po":262,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://docs.mlcommons.org/GaNDLF/itcr_connectivity/#radxtools"}, {"po":262,"n":"Why?","v":"Integration with RadXTools for extended radiology functionality."}, {"po":246,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":246,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Levi Waldron"}, {"po":246,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":246,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/rtracklayer"}, {"po":246,"n":"Why?","v":"The rtracklayer Bioconductor package imports UCSC data and track formats as GenomicRanges objects."}, {"po":231,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":231,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":231,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) IGV"}, {"po":231,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://software.broadinstitute.org/software/igv/book/export/html/6"}, {"po":231,"n":"Why?","v":"BLAT, gene tracks, RefSeq tracks, see IGV manual"}, {"po":230,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":230,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":230,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) Galaxy"}, {"po":230,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/introduction/tutorials/galaxy-intro-strands/tutorial.html"}, {"po":230,"n":"Why?","v":"genomes, too many tools to list here, first tutorial starts with a UCSC browser intro"}, {"po":229,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":229,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":229,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) JBrowse"}, {"po":229,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13059-023-02914-z/tables/2"}, {"po":229,"n":"Why?","v":"UCSC file formats bigBed, bigWig, 2bit and ucsc-to-json script can convert ucsc annotations directly to jbrowse"}, {"po":228,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":228,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":228,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) BRCA Exchange"}, {"po":228,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://brcaexchange.org/variant/788630"}, {"po":228,"n":"Why?","v":"makes data available as a UCSC hub and provides a UCSC browser hub link on every variant page"}, {"po":227,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":227,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":227,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":227,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://store.opencravat.org/manifest-0.0.140.yml"}, {"po":227,"n":"Why?","v":"various connectors import from the UCSC browser, see the connector yaml page"}, {"po":226,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":226,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Max Haeussler"}, {"po":226,"n":"name","v":"UCSC Genome Browser (interacts with) CIViC"}, {"po":226,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://civic.readthedocs.io/en/latest/about/data-clients.html"}, {"po":226,"n":"Why?","v":"Available on UCSC Genome Browser"}, {"po":223,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":223,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Michael Reich"}, {"po":223,"n":"name","v":"g2nb (Connected with) GenePattern"}, {"po":223,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.g2nb.org/tools/"}, {"po":223,"n":"Why?","v":"g2nb is the next evolution of GenePattern Notebook. It has been extended to include multiple bioinformatics tools within a JupyterLab notebook. These include Galaxy, IGV, NDEx, and Cytoscape as well as GenePattern."}, {"po":222,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":222,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Michael Reich"}, {"po":222,"n":"name","v":"g2nb (Connected with) Globus"}, {"po":222,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.g2nb.org/tools/"}, {"po":222,"n":"Why?","v":"g2nb is the next evolution of GenePattern Notebook. It has been extended to include multiple bioinformatics tools within a JupyterLab notebook. These include Galaxy, IGV, NDEx, and Cytoscape as well as GenePattern."}, {"po":221,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":221,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Michael Reich"}, {"po":221,"n":"name","v":"g2nb (Connected with) IGV"}, {"po":221,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.g2nb.org/tools/"}, {"po":221,"n":"Why?","v":"g2nb is the next evolution of GenePattern Notebook. It has been extended to include multiple bioinformatics tools within a JupyterLab notebook. These include Galaxy, IGV, NDEx, and Cytoscape as well as GenePattern."}, {"po":220,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":220,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Michael Reich"}, {"po":220,"n":"name","v":"g2nb (Connected with) Galaxy"}, {"po":220,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.g2nb.org/tools/"}, {"po":220,"n":"Why?","v":"g2nb is the next evolution of GenePattern Notebook. It has been extended to include multiple bioinformatics tools within a JupyterLab notebook. These include Galaxy, IGV, NDEx, and Cytoscape as well as GenePattern."}, {"po":215,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":215,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Christine Micheel"}, {"po":215,"n":"name","v":"MCG (Connected with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":215,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.cbioportal.org/results/mutations?cancer_study_list=pancan_pcawg_2020&Z_SCORE_THRESHOLD=2.0&RPPA_SCORE_THRESHOLD=2.0&profileFilter=mutations%2Ccna&case_set_id=pancan_pcawg_2020_cnaseq&gene_list=EGFR&geneset_list=%20&tab_index=tab_visualize&Action=Submit https://www.cbioportal.org/results/mutations?cancer_study_list=pancan_pcawg_2020&Z_SCORE_THRESHOLD=2.0&RPPA_SCORE_THRESHOLD=2.0&profileFilter=mutations%2Ccna&case_set_id=pancan_pcawg_2020_cnaseq&gene_list=EGFR&geneset_list=%20&tab_index=tab_visualize&Action=Submit"}, {"po":215,"n":"Why?","v":"An ITCR R21 award to Travis Osterman and Christine Micheel uses MCG content. MCG was the first precision oncology knowledgebase and is widely used worldwide. Connections to cBioPortal and the UCSC Genome Browser have existed for many years."}, {"po":214,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":214,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Christine Micheel"}, {"po":214,"n":"name","v":"MCG (Connected with) HemOnc"}, {"po":214,"n":"Why?","v":"MCG and HemOnc have discussed connecting their databases for several years. With both sets of PIs having ITCR-funded grants, this becomes even more likely to occur in the near future."}, {"po":213,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":213,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Jeremy Goecks, Greg Caporaso"}, {"po":213,"n":"name","v":"QIIME-2 (Connected with) Galaxy"}, {"po":213,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://cancer.usegalaxy.org/"}, {"po":213,"n":"Why?","v":"Enables QIIME 2 users to access tools through GUI using Galaxy project hardware; brings many new tools to Galaxy users"}, {"po":212,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":212,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Mary Goldman & Avi Ma'ayan"}, {"po":212,"n":"name","v":"Appyters (Connected with) UCSC Xena"}, {"po":212,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/ucscXena/Xena_DE_Analysis_Pipeline/blob/master/Xena_DE_Analysis_Pipeline.ipynb"}, {"po":212,"n":"Why?","v":"Appyter provides web-based genome-wide analyses for Xena's users"}, {"po":211,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":211,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Andrey Ivanov"}, {"po":211,"n":"name","v":"Averon Notebook (Connected with) NDEx"}, {"po":211,"n":"Why?","v":"The established NDEx REST API and a wide collection of add-on scripts enable rapid and flexible integration of NDEx with the Averon Notebook to facilitate the discovery of actionable vulnerabilities enabled by rewired oncogenic networks. Meanwhile, the predicting functionality of the Averon would open new opportunities for NDEx and Cytoscape users to identify druggable vulnerabilities in cancer functional and protein-protein interaction networks. The interconnection of our tools and complementary expertise of our teams will substantially inform the network analyses and contribute to the systematic discovery of new cancer targets."}, {"po":232,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":232,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Bruno De Man"}, {"po":232,"n":"name","v":"XCIST (Connected with) TCIA"}, {"po":232,"n":"Why?","v":"To support a submitted NIH proposal to use TCIA data with XCIST and to contribute data to TCIA"}, {"po":210,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":210,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Bruno De Man"}, {"po":210,"n":"name","v":"XCIST (connected with) TOPAS"}, {"po":210,"n":"Why?","v":"Combined simulation of imaging (XCIST) and therapy (TOPAS)"}, {"po":209,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":209,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Bruno De Man"}, {"po":209,"n":"name","v":"XCIST (connected with) DICOM ToolKit (DCMTK)"}, {"po":209,"n":"Why?","v":"XCIST can read and write DCM images"}, {"po":280,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":280,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters"}, {"po":280,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) Bioconductor"}, {"po":280,"n":"Why?","v":"Distribute CEDAR as part of Bioconductor’s suite of interoperable bioinformatics packages, enabling programmatic access and integration with widely used analysis workflows."}, {"po":279,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":279,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters "}, {"po":279,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":279,"n":"Why?","v":"Enable integration of CEDAR’s curated cancer epitope datasets with cBioPortal’s genomic and clinical data for enhanced exploration of immunogenicity in a cancer genomics context."}, {"po":208,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":208,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters"}, {"po":208,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) CIViC"}, {"po":208,"n":"Why?","v":"Connect CEDAR’s epitope-level annotations with CIViC’s clinical variant interpretations, facilitating cross-referencing between immune response data and clinically relevant cancer variants. immune recognition information in CIViC would benefit all users."}, {"po":207,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":207,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters"}, {"po":207,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":207,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/wh81sh9zfsm0ad6p4xyio/cedar-1.png?rlkey=n0foif1g6tk3h5hbmxi6e52s9&dl=0"}, {"po":207,"n":"Why?","v":"We can connect CEDAR data to further annotate variants in OpenCRAVAT and increase the depth of information for the cancer research community."}, {"po":206,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":206,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters"}, {"po":206,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) pVACTools"}, {"po":206,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pvactools.readthedocs.io/en/docs/tools.html"}, {"po":206,"n":"Why?","v":"pVACtools would benefit from linking up with cancer-specific tools, such as MHC Class I and II epitope prediction, which are being implemented in the CEDAR Analysis Resource to further assist with vaccine candidate predictions."}, {"po":205,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":205,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Alex Sette and Bjoern Peters"}, {"po":205,"n":"name","v":"CEDAR (connected with) TRUST4"}, {"po":205,"n":"Evidence","v":"http://tools.iedb.org/tcrmatch/"}, {"po":205,"n":"Why?","v":"Addition of a post-processing package of TRUST4 to include CEDAR's TCR and BCR annotations will further enhance the depth of information for users. We are connecting this with CEDAR's TCRMatch tool for even better integration, allowing users to identify epitopes in CEDAR for a given TCR, along with RNA sequencing data from TRUST 4."}, {"po":245,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":245,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Malachi Griffith"}, {"po":245,"n":"name","v":"TRUST4 (connected with) pVACTools"}, {"po":245,"n":"Why?","v":"To integrate TCRseq clonotype expansion information into neoantigen priorization and immunological validation. "}, {"po":286,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":286,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Melanie Courtot"}, {"po":286,"n":"name","v":"Overture (interacts with) IO.BIO"}, {"po":286,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/overture-stack/stage/tree/iobio"}, {"po":286,"n":"Why?","v":"Direct integration of IO.BIO for real-time genomic data visualization of BAM files. This integration connects the data management capabilities of our platform with analysis tools both familiar and useful to cancer researchers."}, {"po":218,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":218,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Zinaida Perova"}, {"po":218,"n":"name","v":"Overture (interacts with) CancerModels.Org"}, {"po":218,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.cancermodels.org/validation/validator"}, {"po":218,"n":"Why?","v":"To provide an on-demand, user-friendly and extensible patient-derived cancer model metadata validation service"}, {"po":204,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":204,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Christina Yung"}, {"po":204,"n":"name","v":"Overture (connected with) JBrowse"}, {"po":204,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/overture-stack/prelude/tree/jbrowse-demo"}, {"po":204,"n":"Why?","v":"It's a new data management tool that has joined the ITCR community, and is integrating with JBrowse as one of the visualization tools."}, {"po":203,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":203,"n":"Suggested By","v":"John Quackenbush"}, {"po":203,"n":"name","v":"WebMeV (connected with) Globus"}, {"po":203,"n":"Why?","v":"WebMeV is designed as an interactive, exploratory data tools for Bioinformatics. However, there are still significant and computationally intensive processes that must be performed prior to WebMeV. These pipelines are typically handled in high performance compute clusters (HPCC), and Globus provides a bridge to seamlessly transfer processed data from Globus integrated HPCCs to WebMeV."}, {"po":202,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":202,"n":"Suggested By","v":"John Quackenbush"}, {"po":202,"n":"name","v":"WebMeV (connected with) IGV"}, {"po":202,"n":"Why?","v":"As WebMeV expands capabilities to managing more data types and analyses beyond RNASeq, we would like to incorporate tools to allow visualization of BED files and alignments within WebMeV. To this end, the mature technology of IGV and its javascript implementation provides a web and cloud friendly technology to integrate into WebMeV."}, {"po":201,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":201,"n":"Suggested By","v":"John Quackenbush"}, {"po":201,"n":"name","v":"WebMeV (connected with) SingleCellTK"}, {"po":201,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://webmev.tm4.org/#/about"}, {"po":201,"n":"Why?","v":"WebMeV was designed for bulk RNASeq analysis. With the advent of single cell RNASeq, we aimed to expand WebMeV’s capabilities to single cell. SCTK is a comprehensive R/Bioconductor package for single cell analysis, and we have implemented the tools to seamlessly interact with WebMeV’s UI and pre-existing tools."}, {"po":219,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":219,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Zinaida Perova"}, {"po":219,"n":"name","v":"CancerModels.Org (interacts with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":219,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.cancermodels.org/cbioportal/"}, {"po":219,"n":"Why?","v":"To enable users to visualise and analyse patient-derived cancer models and associated data."}, {"po":200,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":200,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Zinaida Perova"}, {"po":200,"n":"name","v":"CancerModels.Org (connected with) CIViC"}, {"po":200,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://shorturl.at/Zjnpk"}, {"po":200,"n":"Why?","v":"To assess clinical relevance of PDCM model variants"}, {"po":199,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":199,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Zinaida Perova"}, {"po":199,"n":"name","v":"CancerModels.Org (connected with) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":199,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://rb.gy/z18smn"}, {"po":199,"n":"Why?","v":"To visualize mutations in the context of 3D structures and assess their significance"}, {"po":198,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":198,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Zinaida Perova"}, {"po":198,"n":"name","v":"CancerModels.Org (connected with) OncoMX"}, {"po":198,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://bit.ly/47frPf6"}, {"po":198,"n":"Why?","v":"To improve functional interpretation of PDCM model variants"}, {"po":194,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":194,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Bruce Faddegon, Joseph Perl and Harald Paganetti"}, {"po":194,"n":"name","v":"TOPAS (Connected with) 3D Slicer"}, {"po":194,"n":"Evidence","v":"TOPAS connects with 3D Slicer through DICOM RT. The file format of DICOM RT is outside of both of these tools and is well specified. In the case of connectivity between tools that can read and write DICOM-RT, the evidence is trivial – we wrote out a DICOM RT file from TOPAS and viewed it in 3D Slicer. All of the information for creating DICOM RT with TOPAS and/or 3D Slicer and reading it with 3D Slicer and/or TOPAS is available to users of these two tools. We don’t see there’s really any evidence to provide, other than to say we tried it and it works!"}, {"po":194,"n":"Why?","v":"To view dose distributions calculated with TOPAS with an ITCR tool"}, {"po":193,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":193,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Shartak Pati"}, {"po":193,"n":"name","v":"RADxTools (Connected with) CaPTK"}, {"po":193,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://cbica.github.io/CaPTk/ITCR_Connectivity.html#itcr_radxtools"}, {"po":193,"n":"Why?","v":"CaPTk provides the CoLlAGe features through its feature extraction functionality."}, {"po":189,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":189,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pati Shartak"}, {"po":189,"n":"name","v":"FeTS (Connected with) dcmqi"}, {"po":189,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://fets-ai.github.io/Front-End/itcr_connectivity#DCMQI"}, {"po":189,"n":"Why?","v":"FeTS leverages DCMQI for generating DICOM-Seg files from NIfTI file format."}, {"po":188,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":188,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pati Shartak"}, {"po":188,"n":"name","v":"FeTS (Connected with) DICOM ToolKit (DCMTK)"}, {"po":188,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://fets-ai.github.io/Front-End/itcr_connectivity#DCMTK"}, {"po":188,"n":"Why?","v":"FeTS uses DCMTK for DICOM file handling"}, {"po":187,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":187,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pati Shartak"}, {"po":187,"n":"name","v":"FeTS (Conected with) CaPTK"}, {"po":187,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://fets-ai.github.io/Front-End/itcr_connectivity#CaPTk"}, {"po":187,"n":"Why?","v":"CaPTk’s image preprocessing functionality is integrated in FeTS"}, {"po":186,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":186,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pati Shartak"}, {"po":186,"n":"name","v":"FeTS (Connected with) TCIA"}, {"po":186,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://fets-ai.github.io/Front-End/itcr_connectivity#TCIAandIDC"}, {"po":186,"n":"Why?","v":"Preprocessing and segmentation of TCIA data collections"}, {"po":185,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":185,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Pati Shartak"}, {"po":185,"n":"name","v":"LIBRA (Connected with) CaPTK"}, {"po":185,"n":"Why?","v":"LIBRA is available through the CaPTk GUI and CLI"}, {"po":173,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":173,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Michael Reich"}, {"po":173,"n":"name","v":"CAPER (Connected to) GenePattern"}, {"po":173,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://genepattern.ucsd.edu"}, {"po":173,"n":"Why?","v":"The AmpliconSuite's workflow, comprising the Bafna Lab's Amplicon Architect suite of tools, is being made available as GenePattern modules and notebooks"}, {"po":165,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":165,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Ken Chen"}, {"po":165,"n":"name","v":"Texomer (Connected to) NG-CHM"}, {"po":165,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://bioinformatics.mdanderson.org/texomer/BLCA"}, {"po":165,"n":"Why?","v":"Interact with and functionally annotate Texomer-identified variants/genes of discordant DNA copy number and RNA expression levels."}, {"po":164,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":164,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Jeremy Goecks"}, {"po":164,"n":"name","v":"IO.BIO (Connected to) Galaxy"}, {"po":164,"n":"Why?","v":"Work in progress to enable Galaxy users to view their datasets using IO.BIO applications"}, {"po":174,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":174,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Samuel Gamboa"}, {"po":174,"n":"name","v":"pVACTools (Connected to) Bioconductor"}, {"po":174,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/rworkflow/RcwlRecipes/blob/master/Rcwl/tl_pvacseq.R"}, {"po":174,"n":"Why?","v":"There is a pipeline for pvactools neoantigen prediction in the RcwlPipelines package. This was added in the release 3.10 of bioconductor."}, {"po":162,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":162,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Malachi Griffith & Brian Haas"}, {"po":162,"n":"name","v":"pVACTools (Connected to) Trinity"}, {"po":162,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/TrinityCTAT/CTAT-pVACseq/wiki"}, {"po":162,"n":"Why?","v":"Collaborative set aside will be used to mine neoantigens from genomic events found by Trinity_CTAT and support neoantigen prediction based on RNA-seq identified cancer mutations"}, {"po":161,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":161,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Malachi Griffith"}, {"po":161,"n":"name","v":"pVACTools (Connected to) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":161,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://pvactools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/pvacview/features.html"}, {"po":161,"n":"Why?","v":"OpenCRAVAT is planning to show neoantigen potential from pVACtools as a type of variant annotation. -\tFor neoantigen candidates in the pVACtools submodule \"pVACview\", we link to the corresponding openCRAVAT report."}, {"po":175,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":175,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Chloe Mirzayi"}, {"po":175,"n":"name","v":"BRCA Exchange (Connected to) Bioconductor"}, {"po":175,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.13/bioc/html/GA4GHclient.html"}, {"po":175,"n":"Why?","v":"BRCA exchange makes use of the GA4GH genomics API standards making these data accessible and importable as Bioconductor objects via the GA4GHclient package"}, {"po":159,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":159,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Melissa Cline"}, {"po":159,"n":"name","v":"BRCA Exchange (interacts with) Galaxy"}, {"po":159,"n":"Why?","v":"Proposed collaboration in BRCA Exchange set-aside proposal for federated analysis of Fanconi Anemia data, just underway"}, {"po":158,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":158,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Melissa Cline"}, {"po":158,"n":"name","v":"BRCA Exchange (interacts with) OpenCRAVAT"}, {"po":158,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://brcaexchange.org/variant/508557"}, {"po":158,"n":"Why?","v":"Integration of the CRAVAT MuPIT 3D protein viewer into the BRCA Exchange display"}, {"po":155,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":155,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Leili Shahriyari"}, {"po":155,"n":"name","v":"TumorDecon (Connected with) GSEA/MSigDB"}, {"po":155,"n":"Why?","v":"Tumors consist of many different cell types, including various immune cells, fibroblasts and epithelial cells, and each tumor has its own unique variation of immune cells resulting in different responses to the same treatments. TumorDecon software includes several deconvolution methods and signature matrixes of various cell types. The input of this software is the gene expression profile of the tumor, and the output is the relative number of each cell type"}, {"po":154,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":154,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Leili Shahriyari"}, {"po":154,"n":"name","v":"TumorDecon (Connected with) UCSC Xena"}, {"po":154,"n":"Why?","v":"Tumors consist of many different cell types, including various immune cells, fibroblasts and epithelial cells, and each tumor has its own unique variation of immune cells resulting in different responses to the same treatments. TumorDecon software includes several deconvolution methods and signature matrixes of various cell types. The input of this software is the gene expression profile of the tumor, and the output is the relative number of each cell type"}, {"po":153,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":153,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Leili Shahriyari"}, {"po":153,"n":"name","v":"TumorDecon (Connected with) cBioPortal"}, {"po":153,"n":"Why?","v":"Tumors consist of many different cell types, including various immune cells, fibroblasts and epithelial cells, and each tumor has its own unique variation of immune cells resulting in different responses to the same treatments. TumorDecon software includes several deconvolution methods and signature matrixes of various cell types. The input of this software is the gene expression profile of the tumor, and the output is the relative number of each cell type"}, {"po":281,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":281,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Tin Nguyen"}, {"po":281,"n":"name","v":"GSEA/MSigDB (connected with) IPSA"}, {"po":281,"n":"Why?","v":"IPSA employs multiple pathway analysis methods, including GSEA"}, {"po":176,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":176,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Samuel Gamboa"}, {"po":176,"n":"name","v":"GSEA/MSigDB (Connected to) Bioconductor"}, {"po":176,"n":"Evidence","v":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/experiment/html/msigdb.html"}, {"po":176,"n":"Why?","v":"The MSigDB package provides the Molecular Signatures Database (MSigDB) in a R accessible object"}, {"po":172,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":172,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Helga"}, {"po":172,"n":"name","v":"GSEA/MSigDB (Connected to) NG-CHM"}, {"po":172,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb/human/annotate.jsp"}, {"po":172,"n":"Why?","v":"To integrate the interactive NG-CHM heatmap viewer into the MSigDB online tools"}, {"po":134,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":134,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Helga Thorsvaldottir"}, {"po":134,"n":"name","v":"GSEA/MSigDB (Connected with) GenePattern"}, {"po":134,"n":"Evidence","v":"GSEA is one of the analyses included with GenePattern"}, {"po":133,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":133,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Dexter Pratt"}, {"po":133,"n":"name","v":"GSEA/MSigDB (Connected with) NDEx"}, {"po":133,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb/annotate.jsp"}, {"po":133,"n":"Why?","v":"The NDEx and MSigDB projects are collaborating to integrate their two resources, enabling NDEx users to find gene sets relevant to their networks and vice versa, for MSigDB users to find networks relevant to their gene sets."}, {"po":195,"n":"Status","v":"Exists"}, {"po":195,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Lee Cooper"}, {"po":195,"n":"name","v":"HistoQC connecteds with) CDSA"}, {"po":195,"n":"Evidence","v":"https://github.com/DigitalSlideArchive/histoqc-dsa-plugin"}, {"po":195,"n":"Why?","v":"DSA has integrated HistoQC as a plugin."}, {"po":171,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":171,"n":"Suggested By","v":"???"}, {"po":171,"n":"name","v":"HemOnc (Connected to) cBioPortal"}, {"po":171,"n":"Why?","v":"???"}, {"po":127,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":127,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Jeremy Warner"}, {"po":127,"n":"name","v":"HemOnc (Connected with) DeepPhe"}, {"po":127,"n":"Why?","v":"To add to the existing ontologies and enable identification of chemotherapy regimens."}, {"po":287,"n":"Status","v":"Proposed"}, {"po":287,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Harry Hochheiser"}, {"po":287,"n":"name","v":"DeepPhe (interacts with) GEARBOx"}, {"po":287,"n":"Why?","v":"We are developing ontological models of cancer treatment regimens that might be of use to the gearbox project. Their domain knowledge will contribute to our model development"}, {"po":260,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":260,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Harry Hochheiser"}, {"po":260,"n":"name","v":"DeepPhe (connected with) EMERSE"}, {"po":260,"n":"Why?","v":"Integration of DeepPhe capabilities into EMERSE"}, {"po":259,"n":"Status","v":"Ongoing"}, {"po":259,"n":"Suggested By","v":"Harry 